[decoded] "Based on the notes provided, here is the summary of how this hybrid model processes a token:\n\n*   **State Management:** The model uses a recurrent state per value head instead of a key-value cache, where the state decays by a learned factor at every position.\n*   **Rank-One Updates:** At each position, the key retrieves the predicted state, and the difference between the value and that prediction (scaled by a learned rate) is written back as a rank-one update.\n*   **Attention Mechanism:** Three such layers alternate with one full attention layer, which attends over every earlier position using a partial rotary embedding on a quarter of each head.\n\n**Part that grows with the length of the context:**\nThe **recurrent state** (specifically the state decay and the rank-one updates) grows with the length of the context."
